WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.260
Ryan Murphy, you son of a bitch.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.320
"You son of a bitch."

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:10.060
Yes, another season of "American Horror Story"
has come to an end and I'll be perfectly honest:

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.500
I really enjoyed it.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.820
If you like the campiness, pardon the pun,

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.000
and if you're also like me who grew up
watching cheesy '80s slasher movies,

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.180
this season was such a
fun homage to those films.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.840
I would even put this season in my Top 3.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.420
Yes, I know that statement will
automatically get me some dislikes.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.580
That being said, the ending,
although good, was not great,

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.200
leaving a lot to be desired
both plot- and character-wise.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.540
So in this video, I'm gonna go over how
"American Horror Story: 1984" should have ended.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.140
"Five, six, seven, eight!"

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.740
Now before we get into this new ending,

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:51.140
we have to go over an important ground rule:
episode one to eight will remain unchanged.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:54.360
This isn't because I think they're
perfect, that's not the case at all,

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.280
it's just that if I started cherry-picking
things here and there to change,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.040
this video would get super
complicated and I want to avoid that.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.560
Now that we've got that out of the way,

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.680
we need to focus on those aspects of
the finale that I think need to be changed.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.360
And I'll focus more on broad criticisms
than nitpicking minor things like,

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.920
Oh, I wish Xavier had more air time.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.860
I see you Cody Fern fans out there.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.440
My three main criticisms are as follows:

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.060
One, the curse of Camp Redwood
was never fully explored or resolved.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:30.500
Two, some of the most important character arcs,
namely Brooke and Ricky, were deeply unsatisfying.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.520
And finally, the lack of
tie-ins to other AHS seasons.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.040
The curse of Camp
Redwood is an enigma to me,

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:43.000
with rules that seem to switch episode to episode in order for certain plot points to be hit by the writers.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.440
Like how long does it
take for a body to resurrect?

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.460
That kind of changes
throughout the season.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.740
How can Lavinia seemingly teleport?

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.640
Where did Jingles go
at the end of episode 8?

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:57.200
For now, let's focus on what we do know about
this curse and build our ending around that.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:03.640
One, it started in 1948 with the death of Bobby
Richter and her mother's subsequent murder spree,

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.700
resulting in Benjamin
killing his own mother.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:12.960
This is why we don't have any super old-timey ghosts, which would hint that the curse goes way before '48.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.960
After the massacre and death of Lavinia,

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.440
anyone killed within the Camp Redwood property
is resurrected as a ghost for all eternity.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.580
It's essentially their own limbo.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:27.640
In the current ending, there's no real resolution
to this curse, when I think there should be.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:33.800
If Lavinia gets Bobby back and patches things up
with Ben, the curse theoretically should be lifted.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.300
But the ending we got, the
campers were still stuck at Redwood.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.160
We'll get to how I'll change this in a bit.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:43.860
Character arcs were also a big problem
for me, mainly those of Brooke and Ricky.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.580
Brooke starts off the
season as our main protagonist,

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:50.680
yet the final episode has her hiding
away, marrying a dermatologist,

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:57.320
and her only real purpose in the episode is to exposition-dump everything that happened to her since 1989.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:02.100
Ricky, although he doesn't have quite an arc, since
his character is pretty static throughout the season,

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.640
didn't get an ending
worthy of his evil character.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.500
By that I mean he could
have gotten it a lot worse.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.760
Now I don't mean physically, since
his death was quite brutal, but emotionally.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.960
An emotional betrayal of sorts by someone
he admires more than anyone else.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.300
We'll get to that too.

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:22.740
And finally the ending missed some great
opportunities to tie in previous AHS seasons.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:27.200
AHS is known for connecting tons of characters
from different seasons to one another,

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.680
and I think they could have
exploited this much more,

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.760
particularly Ricky's relationship to
Satan tying in to "Apocalypse."

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.480
Okay, you've heard my critiques, now I'm gonna
show you how I think this season should have ended.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:43.340
Keep in mind my ending is batshit
insane, but hey, so was the season.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.200
It likely has its own
problems, I wrote this in a day,

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.460
and it likely wouldn't happen due to,
well, you'll just have to keep watching.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:51.860
Let's get into it.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:58.440
We start just like the original ending: a grown up
Bobby Richter has arrived at Camp Redwood in 2019,

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.680
searching for answers about his father.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:07.000
Whereas the original has him meet Montana and
Trevor, in my version he meets Jingles, his dad.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:12.640
One of the things I didn't like about the original was
that Bobby and Jingles hug once and that's about it.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:16.360
In my way, it allows them to
connect a bit more before the big finale,

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:22.320
so that when things finally get resolved, we feel more attached to them and it's more emotional, less forced.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:27.720
Well, Jingles will go on to say that he and the
other ghosts are stuck for eternity at Camp Redwood.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:30.140
Their souls will never be at rest.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:34.300
The curse was supposed to be lifted
when Lavinia was reunited with Bobby,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:40.580
but some evil force is preventing the ghosts, aka
the other campers and counselors, from moving on.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:46.040
It's here the other ghosts reveal themselves
to Bobby as we flash back to 1989

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.000
to hear the story of what
happened at the festival.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.580
Trevor will have blocked the road,
preventing the festival goers from getting in,

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:57.300
but it's here none other than
Billy Idol arrives in his tour bus,

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:01.560
played, of course, by Evan Peters, but
someone else should he not be available.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.060
He's flown all the way
from the UK and is pissed.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.180
What do you mean
the festival's canceled?

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:11.700
He gave up a meeting with the Queen
to be here. Will he still be getting paid?

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:17.280
He storms past Trevor onto the Camp Redwood
grounds in search of Margaret, demanding answers.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:24.160
I like this version, because the original built up Billy Idol for almost three episodes and there was no payoff.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:29.100
Billy can also be used plot-wise to manipulate
Ricky, since we know how much he loves him.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.840
"Billy Idol's the truth, man."

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:36.160
Montana will exploit this by telling Ricky
she's arranged a private meeting with him,

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.940
away from all the other less devoted fans,

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.840
and this could take place in Lavinia's shack
where the other ghosts wait for him,

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:45.400
trapping him in there
similar to the original.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:49.640
We flash forward back to present day
where Jingles brings his son to see Ricky,

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:54.540
who they have tied up and confined in his
own satanic cell for the past 30 years.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.920
This scene could be fun since
you'll have Ricky taunting Bobby,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.300
saying he'll get his revenge and saying
how he enjoyed carving up his mother,

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.940
but the real purpose of this
scene is to highlight how

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:10.560
whatever satanic power is trapped within
Ricky is preventing the curse from being lifted.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.560
The ghosts have tried everything,

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:16.760
but Ricky keeps coming back to life
with his satanic spirit trapped within him.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:21.860
If they can somehow remove this demonic force
from his body, maybe they can break the curse.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:27.100
In the meantime, they've done the only thing they
can: keep him confined so he can't escape Redwood.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.880
Bobby is now determined.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:32.520
He says he'll find a way to lift the
curse and save the other ghosts.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.900
After all, it was his
father and the other ghosts

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.040
who have been protecting him in the world
all these years from the evil that is Ricky.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.600
It's the least he can do.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:45.180
Jingles tells Bobby to start his quest with
Donna Chambers at the Red Meadows Asylum.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.200
She may have some answers.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:50.620
Bobby visits Donna at the asylum,
similar to how he did in the original.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:54.460
Here, we'll have Donna recount how Brooke
and her got the revenge and killed Margaret,

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:58.640
but my version has an injured Brooke
being taken to the camps edge by Ray,

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:04.100
only for her to be saved by none other than
Billy Idol, whose tour bus is still there.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:07.340
As we flash-forward, Bobby
says he thought Brooke didn't survive.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:11.000
He searched everywhere for a Brooke
Thompson, but couldn't find one.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.760
That's because she's no
longer Brooke Thompson.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.520
Are you ready for this? She's Brooke Idol.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:23.220
Yes, the girl who started as a virgin with the
squeaky-clean lifestyle has come full circle,

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.040
marrying one of the most
badass singers in rock'n'roll.

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:31.780
A marriage that would have had to be kept secret, since Brooke is still considered to be dead from death row.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:35.840
Bobby goes to the gates outside Billy's
mansion and is turned away by the guard,

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:40.000
who thinks he's a crazy fan shouting
things about ghosts and Camp Redwood,

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.360
kind of like how he was
turned away at the asylum.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.280
But Brooke will overhear this and bring him
inside, where Bobby will plead with her to go back.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.380
They need to save the
others and stop Ricky for good.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.180
The curse of Redwood needs to be lifted.

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:55.020
And he doesn't know who to turn to.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:59.140
Back at Redwood, a few days later,
Chet and Bertie are on the night shift,

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.500
looking after Ricky, just like the original,

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.820
when they are viciously
murdered by none other than Billy Idol.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.900
But as we'll find out, spoiler alert,

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.620
this is all part of the plan.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:12.060
It's not a big deal to kill Chet and Bertie,
since they'll just resurrect again.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.800
Ricky is astonished to see his true hero
helping him out of his confinement,

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:21.000
Billy saying that Satan talked to
him and ordered him to set Ricky free,

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:23.000
that Satan isn't done with him.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:28.920
Billy tells him a boat is waiting for them at the dock and that they'll finally be free once they get off the property.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:32.620
As they get down to the dock,
Ricky remarks, "Where's the boat?"

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:37.300
But it's all a trap, revealing
Cordelia at the other end of the dock.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:40.740
Yes, the Cordelia Goode
from "Coven" and "Apocalypse."

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:43.740
If there's anyone who can
deal with satanic beings it's her,

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.220
and you know I had to
bring our girl Paulson back.

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:50.020
As we'll find out, Billy is actually a
warlock who attended Hawthorne,

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.660
hence how he would know Cordelia,

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:55.160
and we could also tie this
into his success as a rockstar.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:09:01.340
Cordelia will cast a spell, lifting Ricky into the air as
the demonic spirit escapes from his throat and mouth.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:05.680
The other ghost from the season emerge from
the forest, watching as these events unfold,

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.420
including both Bobby, Jingles,
Lavinia, and Bobby Jr., all side by side.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:13.620
With a final blow, the
demonic entity is destroyed,

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:17.460
casting the entire lake
and forest in bright white light,

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:20.340
Ricky's body collapsing
on the edge of the dock.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.800
The curse has been lifted
and Ricky is now mortal.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:27.000
Billy takes Ricky's curved
knife, ready to end him for good.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:31.200
It's the biggest betrayal for Ricky,
his hero being the one to kill him,

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:34.440
when Brooke swerves in
and guts him in the stomach.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:38.240
After all, it was Ricky who
first tried to kill her in episode 1.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:42.540
With blood coming out from his mouth,
his face of betrayal turns to an evil smirk

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:47.820
as he recites Billy's lyrics from his song
"Rebel Yell", saying, "More, more, more,"

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.800
as Montana and the other
ghosts stab him mercilessly.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.940
We get a goodbye between Jingles and Bobby,

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:57.540
before a mysterious force slowly pulls
the ghost towards the center of the lake.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:01.980
Cordelia, Bobby, Brooke, and Billy watch
as the ghosts disappear above the lake,

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:06.640
their souls finally put to rest and
the curse of Redwood finally lifted.

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.540
I would have loved to have months
working on a better ending than this one,

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:15.060
but hey, with a half day and not having to worry about whether Evan Peters or Sarah Paulson could come back,

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:19.340
I thought this would be a fun
exercise for all of us AHS fans out there.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:22.760
If you enjoyed it, I would love it if you
gave it a like and made a comment.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:27.840
And make sure to subscribe, since I have tons of
other videos coming up before the next AHS season.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.800
You can also follow me
on Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.480
Until next time remember,

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:34.060
Daddy loves you very much.

